#: paneltab.cpp:101
msgid "&Hide Buttons"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:111
msgid "&Enabled"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:113
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the panel will have buttons on both ends that can "
"be used to hide it. The panel will slide away, leaving more room for "
"applications. There only remains a small button which can be used to show "
"the panel again."
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:118
msgid "Highlight on mouse &over"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:120
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the hide buttons are highlighted when the mouse "
"cursor is moved over them."
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:131
msgid "Size:"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:133
msgid "Here you can change the size of the hide buttons."
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:141
msgid "&Auto Hide"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:147
msgid "En&abled"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:150
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled the panel will automatically hide after some time "
"and reappear when you move the mouse to the screen edge the panel is "
"attached to. This is particularly useful for small screen resolutions, for "
"example, on laptops."
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:156
msgid "&Delay in seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:159
msgid ""
"Here you can change the delay after which the panel will disappear if not "
"used."
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:165
msgid "Mis&cellaneous"
msgstr ""

#: paneltab.cpp:172
msgid "Terminal application:"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:56
msgid "&Hide Animation"
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:77 buttontab.cpp:106 buttontab.cpp:135 buttontab.cpp:164
#: buttontab.cpp:193 buttontab.cpp:222 lnftab.cpp:62 lnftab.cpp:85
msgid "Enabled"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:65
msgid ""
"If hide buttons are enabled, check this option to make the panel softly "
"slide away when you click on the hide buttons. Else it will just disappear."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:70 lnftab.cpp:93
msgid "Speed:"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:73
msgid ""
"Determines the speed of the hide animation, i.e. the animation shown when "
"you click on the panel's hide buttons."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:79
msgid "&Auto Hide Animation"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:88
msgid ""
"If auto-hide panel is enabled, check this option to make the panel softly "
"slide down after a certain amount of time. Else it will just disappear."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:96
msgid ""
"Determines the speed of the auto-hide animation, i.e. the animation shown "
"when the panel disappears after a certain amount of time."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:102
msgid "Background Theme"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:109
msgid "Use background theme"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:117
msgid ""
"If this option is selected, you can choose an individual 'theme' that will "
"be used to display the panel. If it is not selected, the default colors will "
"be used, see the 'Colors' control module."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:121
msgid "This is a preview for the selected panel theme."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:127
msgid "Browse"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:129
msgid ""
"Here you can choose a theme to be displayed by the panel. Press the 'Browse' "
"button to choose a theme using the file dialog.<p> This option is only "
"active if 'Use background theme' is selected."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:151
msgid "Fade out applet handles"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:154
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the handle on the left of a panel applet will "
"only be shown when the mouse cursor is moved over it."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:183
msgid "Select a image file"
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:200
msgid "Failed to load image file."
msgstr ""

#: lnftab.cpp:251 lnftab.cpp:254
msgid "Error loading theme image file."
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:50 menutab.cpp:44
msgid "General"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:50
msgid "Clear menu cache"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:53
msgid ""
"The panel can cache information about menu entries instead of reading it "
"from disk every time you browse the menus. This makes the panel menus react "
"faster. However, you might want to turn this off if you're short on memory."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:59
msgid "Clear after n seconds:"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:62
msgid ""
"If menu chaching is turned on, you can set a delay after which the cache "
"will be cleared."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:68
msgid "Browser Menus"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:74
msgid "Show hidden files"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:77
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, hidden files (i.e. files beginning with a dot) "
"will be shown in the QuickBrowser menus."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:82
msgid "Maximum browser menu entries:"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:85
msgid ""
"When browsing directories that contain a lot of files, the QuickBrowser can "
"sometimes hide your whole desktop. Here you can limit the number of entries "
"shown at a time in the QuickBrowser. This is particularly useful for low "
"screen resolutions."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:92
msgid "K Menu"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:98
msgid "Merge different menu locations"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:102
msgid ""
"KDE can support several different locations on the system for storing "
"program information, including (but not limited to) a system-wide and a "
"personal directory. Enabling this option makes the KDE panel merge these "
"different locations into a single logical tree of programs."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:110
msgid "Show bookmarks submenu"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:113
msgid ""
"Enabling this option will make the panel show a bookmarks menu in your KDE "
"menu"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:116
msgid "Show recent documents submenu"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:119
msgid ""
"Enabling this option will make the panel show a recent documents menu in "
"your KDE menu, containing shortcuts to your most recently edited documents. "
"This assumes you've been using KDE applications to edit those documents, as "
"other applications will not be able to take advantage of this feature."
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:124
msgid "Show quickbrowser submenu"
msgstr ""

#: menutab.cpp:127
msgid ""
"Enabling this option will show the 'Quick Browser' in your KDE menu, a fast "
"way of accessing your files via submenus. You can also add a Quick Browser "
"as a panel button, using the panel context menu."
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:56
msgid "Enable background tiles"
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:59
msgid ""
"If this option is enabled, the panel will display panel buttons using tile "
"images instead of just drawing flat buttons. You can still enable or disable "
"usage of tiles for the different kind of panel buttons, using the options "
"below."
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:67
msgid "K-Menu Tiles"
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:83
msgid "Enable or disable the usage of a tile image for the K menu."
msgstr ""

#: buttontab.cpp:84
